Q: Why is this phone number not recognised in iOS Safari? A: <hr />
<p>The issue occurs because Safari's pattern recognition can be inconsistent when phone numbers are mixed with specific keywords like &quot;Bound&quot;. To fix this and ensure 100% reliability, you should take manual control.</p>
<p><strong>1. Disable Auto-Detection</strong> Add this meta tag to your <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> section to stop Safari from guessing:</p>
<p>HTML</p>
<pre><code>&lt;meta name=&quot;format-detection&quot; content=&quot;telephone=no&quot;&gt;
</code></pre>
<p><strong>2. Use Manual <code>tel:</code> Links</strong> Wrap your phone numbers in an anchor tag. This is the standard way to ensure it works across all mobile browsers:</p>
<p>HTML</p>
<pre><code>&lt;p&gt;Bound &lt;a href=&quot;tel:1-555-555-5555&quot;&gt;1-555-555-5555&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</code></pre>
<p><strong>3. Style for Consistency (CSS)</strong> Use this CSS to prevent the default blue link style while keeping it interactive on mobile:</p>
<p>CSS</p>
<pre><code>a[href^=&quot;tel&quot;] {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
}

@media (max-width: 768px) {
    a[href^=&quot;tel&quot;] {
        color: #007bff;
        text-decoration: underline;
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p><strong>Demo:</strong> You can check the fix here <a href="https://codepen.io/aymandevoffical-stack/pen/pvEYRRK" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://codepen.io/aymandevoffical-stack/pen/pvEYRRK</a></p>

Q: How would i sign a user out once the jwt token expires in react? A: <p>To implement session expiration in React, the best approach is to combine the <strong>JWT's <code>exp</code> (expiration) claim</strong> with a <strong><code>useEffect</code> hook</strong> in your top-level component.</p>
<p>While <code>localStorage</code> is simple, it is passive; it cannot &quot;listen&quot; for time. You must actively check the token status.</p>
<p>Use a wrapper component (a &quot;Guard&quot;) or a <code>useEffect</code> in your <code>App.jsx</code> to verify the token status.</p>
<p>The code is as follows:</p>
<pre><code>import { useEffect } from 'react';
import { useNavigate, useLocation } from 'react-router-dom';
import { jwtDecode } from 'jwt-decode'; // npm install jwt-decode

const SessionManager = () =&gt; {
  const navigate = useNavigate();
  const location = useLocation();

  useEffect(() =&gt; {
    const checkToken = () =&gt; {
      const token = localStorage.getItem('token');
      if (!token) return;

      const { exp } = jwtDecode(token);
      const isExpired = Date.now() &gt;= exp * 1000;

      if (isExpired) {
        localStorage.removeItem('token');
        navigate('/login');
      }
    };

    // Check on route change
    checkToken();
  }, [location, navigate]);

  return null; // This component doesn't render anything
};
</code></pre>
